### Description
This Terraform program sets up an AWS Elastic Beanstalk environment with autoscaling based on CPU utilization, connected to an RDS database. It includes the necessary IAM roles and instance profiles for the EC2 instances in the Elastic Beanstalk environment. The program ensures that all dependencies are correctly managed and that the resources are properly configured.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

# IAM Role for EC2 instances in Elastic Beanstalk
resource "aws_iam_role" "eb_ec2_role" {
  name = "eb_ec2_role"

  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Action = "sts:AssumeRole"
        Effect = "Allow"
        Principal = {
          Service = "ec2.amazonaws.com"
        }
      }
    ]
  })
}

# IAM Instance Profile associated with the IAM role
resource "aws_iam_instance_profile" "eb_ec2_profile" {
  name = "eb_ec2_profile"
  roles = [aws_iam_role.eb_ec2_role.name]
}

# RDS Database instance
