### Description
The Terraform program below creates an AWS Elastic Beanstalk Web Server environment with an associated Elastic Beanstalk application. It also sets up an IAM role (`eb_ec2_role`) and an instance profile (`eb_ec2_profile`) required for the EC2 instances in the Elastic Beanstalk environment. The program ensures that all dependencies are correctly handled and that the necessary permissions are assigned to the IAM role.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"  # Specify your desired AWS region
}

# IAM Role for EC2 instances in Elastic Beanstalk
resource "aws_iam_role" "eb_ec2_role" {
  name = "eb_ec2_role"

  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Action = "sts:AssumeRole"
        Effect = "Allow"
        Principal = {
          Service = "ec2.amazonaws.com"
        }
      }
    ]
  })
}

# IAM Instance Profile associated with the IAM role
resource "aws_iam_instance_profile" "eb_ec2_profile" {
  name = "eb_ec2_profile"
  roles = [aws_iam_role.eb_ec2_role.name]
}

# Elastic Beanstalk Application
resource "aws_elastic_beanstalk_application" "my_application" {
  name        = "my_application"
  description = "My Elastic Beanstalk Application"
}

# Elastic Beanstalk Environment
resource "aws_elastic_beanstalk_environment" "my_webserver_environment" {
  name                = "my-webserver-environment"
  application         = aws_elastic_beanstalk_application.my_application.name
  solution_stack_name = "64bit Amazon Linux 2 v3.5.0 running Python 3.8"

  setting {
    namespace = "aws:autoscaling:launchconfiguration"
    name      = "IamInstanceProfile"
    value     = aws_iam_instance_profile.eb_ec2_profile.name
  }

  setting {
    namespace = "aws:ec2:instances"
    name      = "InstanceType"
    value     = "t2.micro"
  }
}
```

### Explanation
1. **Provider Configuration**: The AWS provider is configured with a specific region (`us-west-2`).
2. **IAM Role (`eb_ec2_role`)**: An IAM role is created with a trust policy allowing EC2 to assume the role.
3. **IAM Instance Profile (`eb_ec2_profile`)**: An instance profile is created and associated with the IAM role.
4. **Elastic Beanstalk Application (`my_application`)**: An Elastic Beanstalk application is created with a description.
5. **Elastic Beanstalk Environment (`my_webserver_environment`)**: An Elastic Beanstalk environment is created, linked to the application, and configured with a solution stack and settings for the instance type and IAM instance profile.

This configuration ensures that all resources are properly set up and interconnected according to the provided IaC Intent Graph IR.

