### Description

The Terraform program below defines a Kendra data source resource with URL exclusion and inclusion patterns. It also creates an IAM role and attaches a policy to that role, ensuring that the Kendra data source has the necessary permissions to access its data source.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"  # Specify your desired AWS region
}

variable "kendra_index_id" {
  description = "The ID of the Kendra index"
  type        = string
}

variable "data_source_name" {
  description = "The name of the Kendra data source"
  type        = string
  default     = "my_kendra_data_source"
}

variable "url_exclusion_patterns" {
  description = "List of URL exclusion patterns"
  type        = list(string)
  default     = []
}

variable "url_inclusion_patterns" {
  description = "List of URL inclusion patterns"
  type        = list(string)
  default     = []
}

resource "aws_iam_role" "kendra_role" {
  name = "kendra_role"

  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Action = "sts:AssumeRole"
        Effect = "Allow"
        Principal = {
          Service = "kendra.amazonaws.com"
        }
      }
    ]
  })
}

resource "aws_iam_role_policy" "kendra_role_policy" {
  name   = "kendra_role_policy"
  role   = aws_iam_role.kendra_role.id
  policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Action = [
          "s3:GetObject",
          "s3:ListBucket"
        ]
        Effect = "Allow"
        Resource = [
          "arn:aws:s3:::your-bucket-name",  # Replace with your S3 bucket ARN
          "arn:aws:s3:::your-bucket-name/*" # Replace with your S3 bucket ARN
        ]
      }
    ]
  })
}

resource "aws_kendra_data_source" "kendra_data_source" {
  depends_on = [aws_iam_role.kendra_role]

  name         = var.data_source_name
  index_id     = var.kendra_index_id
  type         = "WEBSITE"
  role_arn     = aws_iam_role.kendra_role.arn

  website_configuration {
    url = "https://example.com"  # Replace with your website URL

    crawl_depth = 2

    url_exclusion_patterns = var.url_exclusion_patterns
    url_inclusion_patterns = var.url_inclusion_patterns
  }
}
```

### Notes

1. **Provider Configuration**: The AWS provider is configured with a default region (`us-west-2`). You can change this to your preferred region.
2. **Variables**: The program uses several variables to allow customization, such as `kendra_index_id`, `data_source_name`, `url_exclusion_patterns`, and `url_inclusion_patterns`.
3. **IAM Role and Policy**: An IAM role named `kendra_role` is created, and a policy is attached to it allowing access to an S3 bucket. You need to replace `"arn:aws:s3:::your-bucket-name"` with the actual ARN of your S3 bucket.
4. **Kendra Data Source**: The Kendra data source is configured to crawl a website. You need to replace `"https://example.com"` with the actual URL of the website you want to crawl. The `crawl_depth` is set to 2, but you can adjust this as needed. The `url_exclusion_patterns` and `url_inclusion_patterns` are set using the provided variables.

This configuration ensures that the Kendra data source has the necessary permissions to access its data source and respects the specified URL patterns.

