### Description

This Terraform program sets up a non-alias AWS Route 53 record linked to a private Route 53 zone named "internal.example53.com". The private zone is associated with an AWS VPC named "main". The program ensures that the VPC is created before the private zone, and the private zone is created before the Route 53 record.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"  # Specify your desired AWS region
}

resource "aws_vpc" "main" {
  cidr_block = "10.0.0.0/16"
  enable_dns_support   = true
  enable_dns_hostnames = true

  tags = {
    Name = "main_vpc"
  }
}

resource "aws_route53_zone" "private_zone" {
  name       = "internal.example53.com"
  vpc {
    vpc_id = aws_vpc.main.id
  }

  tags = {
    Name = "private_zone"
  }
}

resource "aws_route53_record" "non_alias_record" {
  zone_id = aws_route53_zone.private_zone.zone_id
  name    = "example"
  type    = "A"
  ttl     = 300
  records = ["10.0.1.1"]  # Replace with the desired IP address

  tags = {
    Name = "non_alias_record"
  }
}
```

### Explanation

1. **Provider Configuration**: The AWS provider is configured with a specific region (`us-west-2`). You can change this to your preferred region.

2. **AWS VPC Resource (`aws_vpc.main`)**: A VPC is created with a CIDR block of `10.0.0.0/16`. DNS support and hostnames are enabled.

3. **AWS Route 53 Zone Resource (`aws_route53_zone.private_zone`)**: A private Route 53 zone is created with the name "internal.example53.com" and is associated with the VPC created in the previous step.

4. **AWS Route 53 Record Resource (`aws_route53_record.non_alias_record`)**: A non-alias A record is created within the private zone. The record points to an IP address (`10.0.1.1`), which you should replace with the appropriate IP address for your use case. The record has a TTL of 300 seconds.

This configuration ensures that all resources are created in the correct order and are properly linked.

