### Description

This Terraform program defines an AWS EKS cluster named based on a provided `cluster_name` variable. It creates an IAM role specifically for EKS cluster management and attaches the necessary policies to this role. The EKS cluster is configured with VPC subnet IDs for networking. Local-exec provisioners are used to manage kubectl configuration during the creation and destruction of the EKS cluster.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"  # Specify your desired AWS region
}

variable "cluster_name" {
  type        = string
  description = "The name of the EKS cluster"
  default     = "my-eks-cluster"
}

variable "vpc_subnet_ids" {
  type        = list(string)
  description = "List of VPC subnet IDs for the EKS cluster"
  default     = []  # Provide your subnet IDs here
}

resource "aws_iam_role" "eks_cluster_role" {
  name = "${var.cluster_name}_eks_cluster_role"

  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Action = "sts:AssumeRole"
        Effect = "Allow"
        Principal = {
          Service = "eks.amazonaws.com"
        }
      }
    ]
  })
}

resource "aws_iam_role_policy_attachment" "eks_cluster_policy_attachment" {
  policy_arn = "arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/AmazonEKSClusterPolicy"
  role       = aws_iam_role.eks_cluster_role.name
}

resource "aws_iam_role_policy_attachment" "eks_service_policy_attachment" {
  policy_arn = "arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/AmazonEKSServicePolicy"
  role       = aws_iam_role.eks_cluster_role.name
}

resource "aws_eks_cluster" "eks_cluster" {
  name     = var.cluster_name
  role_arn = aws_iam_role.eks_cluster_role.arn

  vpc_config {
    subnet_ids = var.vpc_subnet_ids
  }

  # Local-exec provisioner to configure kubectl during cluster creation
  provisioner "local-exec" {
    command = "aws eks update-kubeconfig --name ${var.cluster_name}"
  }

  # Local-exec provisioner to clean up kubectl configuration during cluster destruction
  provisioner "local-exec" {
    when    = destroy
    command = "kubectl config delete-context ${var.cluster_name}"
  }
}
```

### Notes

1. **Provider Configuration**: The AWS provider is configured with a default region (`us-west-2`). You can change this to your preferred region.
2. **Variables**: 
   - `cluster_name`: The name of the EKS cluster. Default is `"my-eks-cluster"`.
   - `vpc_subnet_ids`: A list of VPC subnet IDs required for the EKS cluster's networking. You must provide your subnet IDs here.
3. **IAM Role and Policies**: An IAM role is created with policies attached for EKS cluster and service management.
4. **Local-exec Provisioners**: These are used to update and delete kubectl configurations during the creation and destruction of the EKS cluster, respectively.

Make sure to replace the default subnet IDs in the `vpc_subnet_ids` variable with your actual subnet IDs before deploying the Terraform configuration.

