LLM Output #0:
### Description
The Terraform program below creates an AWS SageMaker app configured as a JupyterServer. The program includes the necessary provider configuration and sets up an IAM role with the required permissions for the SageMaker app. The SageMaker app is named `sagemaker_jupyter_server`.

### Terraform HCL Program
```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"  # Ensure this is set to your desired AWS region
}

resource "aws_iam_role" "sagemaker_execution_role" {
  name = "sagemaker-execution-role"

  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Action = "sts:AssumeRole"
        Effect = "Allow"
        Principal = {
          Service = "sagemaker.amazonaws.com"
        }
      }
    ]
  })
}

resource "aws_iam_role_policy_attachment" "sagemaker_full_access" {
  policy_arn = "arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/AmazonSageMakerFullAccess"
  role       = aws_iam_role.sagemaker_execution_role.name
}

resource "aws_sagemaker_app" "sagemaker_jupyter_server" {
  app_name     = "jupyter-server-app"
  app_type     = "JupyterServer"
  domain_id    = var.domain_id  # You need to provide the domain ID
  user_profile_name = var.user_profile_name  # You need to provide the user profile name
  role_arn     = aws_iam_role.sagemaker_execution_role.arn
}

variable "domain_id" {
  description = "The ID of the SageMaker domain where the app will be created."
  type        = string
}

variable "user_profile_name" {
  description = "The name of the user profile associated with the app."
  type        = string
}
```

### Notes
- **Provider Configuration**: The AWS provider is configured with the region `us-west-2`. You can change this to your preferred region.
- **IAM Role**: An IAM role named `sagemaker-execution-role` is created with a trust policy allowing SageMaker to assume it. The role is attached to the `AmazonSageMakerFullAccess` policy.
- **SageMaker App**: A SageMaker app of type `JupyterServer` is created. You need to provide the `domain_id` and `user_profile_name` as variables.
- **Variables**: The `domain_id` and `user_profile_name` are defined as variables with descriptions and types. You must provide these values when deploying the configuration.

