### Description
The Terraform program below creates an AWS SageMaker model using the KMeans algorithm. It includes the necessary IAM role and policy to allow the SageMaker model to execute properly. The program ensures that all dependencies are correctly defined and that the resources are created in the specified order.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"  # Specify your desired AWS region
}

variable "sagemaker_role_name" {
  description = "The name of the SageMaker execution role"
  default     = "sagemaker_execution_role"
}

variable "sagemaker_policy_name" {
  description = "The name of the SageMaker execution policy"
  default     = "sagemaker_execution_policy"
}

variable "sagemaker_model_name" {
  description = "The name of the SageMaker model"
  default     = "kmeans_model"
}

resource "aws_iam_role" "sagemaker_execution_role" {
  name = var.sagemaker_role_name

  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Action = "sts:AssumeRole"
        Effect = "Allow"
        Principal = {
          Service = "sagemaker.amazonaws.com"
        }
      }
    ]
  })
}

resource "aws_iam_role_policy" "sagemaker_execution_policy" {
  name   = var.sagemaker_policy_name
  role   = aws_iam_role.sagemaker_execution_role.id
  policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Action = [
          "s3:GetObject",
          "s3:PutObject",
          "logs:CreateLogGroup",
          "logs:CreateLogStream",
          "logs:PutLogEvents"
        ]
        Effect = "Allow"
        Resource = "*"
      }
    ]
  })
}

resource "aws_sagemaker_model" "kmeans_model" {
  name               = var.sagemaker_model_name
  execution_role_arn = aws_iam_role.sagemaker_execution_role.arn

  primary_container {
    image = "683313688378.dkr.ecr.us-west-2.amazonaws.com/kmeans:latest"
  }
}
```

### Explanation
1. **Provider Configuration**: The AWS provider is configured with the region `us-west-2`. You can change this to your preferred region.
2. **Variables**: Default values are provided for the role name, policy name, and model name.
3. **IAM Role**: An IAM role named `sagemaker_execution_role` is created with a trust policy allowing SageMaker to assume the role.
4. **IAM Role Policy**: A policy named `sagemaker_execution_policy` is attached to the IAM role, granting necessary permissions for S3, CloudWatch Logs, and SageMaker operations.
5. **SageMaker Model**: A SageMaker model named `kmeans_model` is created using the KMeans algorithm image from the AWS ECR repository.

This configuration ensures that all resources are created in the correct order and that the SageMaker model has the necessary permissions to run.

