### Description
The Terraform program below creates an AWS DAX (DynamoDB Accelerator) cluster. The program includes a provider configuration for AWS, specifying the region. It also defines an IAM role required for the DAX cluster to interact with DynamoDB. The DAX cluster is created with default settings, and it depends on the IAM role being available.

### Terraform HCL Program
```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"  # Specify your desired AWS region
}

resource "aws_iam_role" "dax_role" {
  name = "dax_role"

  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Action = "sts:AssumeRole"
        Effect = "Allow"
        Principal = {
          Service = "dax.amazonaws.com"
        }
      }
    ]
  })
}

resource "aws_iam_role_policy_attachment" "dax_policy" {
  policy_arn = "arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/service-role/AmazonDAXFullAccess"
  role       = aws_iam_role.dax_role.name
}

resource "aws_dax_cluster" "dax_cluster" {
  cluster_name       = "my-dax-cluster"
  iam_role_arn       = aws_iam_role.dax_role.arn
  node_type          = "dax.t3.small"
  replication_factor = 1
  subnet_group_name  = "default"  # Ensure this subnet group exists in your VPC

  depends_on = [aws_iam_role_policy_attachment.dax_policy]
}
```

### Notes
- Ensure that the AWS DAX service is enabled in the specified region.
- The `subnet_group_name` should be replaced with an existing subnet group in your VPC.
- The `node_type` and `replication_factor` can be adjusted based on your performance and availability requirements.
- The IAM role and policy attachment ensure that the DAX cluster has the necessary permissions to access DynamoDB.

