### Description
This Terraform program sets up a basic AWS Neptune cluster with a custom parameter group and an instance in that cluster with its own custom parameter group. The Neptune instance is configured to only allow connections from a specified subnet. The program includes the necessary resources and dependencies as outlined in the IaC Intent Graph IR.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"  # Specify your desired AWS region
}

# Define a subnet group for Neptune instances
resource "aws_neptune_subnet_group" "neptune_subnet_group" {
  name       = "neptune-subnet-group"
  subnet_ids = var.subnet_ids  # Provide a list of subnet IDs

  tags = {
    Name = "NeptuneSubnetGroup"
  }
}

# Create a custom parameter group for the Neptune cluster
resource "aws_neptune_cluster_parameter_group" "neptune_cluster_parameter_group" {
  family = "neptune1"

  parameter {
    name         = "neptune_query_timeout"
    value        = "30"
    apply_method = "immediate"
  }

  tags = {
    Name = "NeptuneClusterParameterGroup"
  }
}

# Create a Neptune cluster using the defined subnet group and parameter group
resource "aws_neptune_cluster" "neptune_cluster" {
  cluster_identifier                  = "neptune-cluster"
  engine                              = "neptune"
  engine_version                      = "1.2.0.1"
  backup_retention_period             = 5
  preferred_backup_window             = "07:00-09:00"
  skip_final_snapshot                 = true
  iam_database_authentication_enabled = true

  neptune_subnet_group_name = aws_neptune_subnet_group.neptune_subnet_group.name
  neptune_cluster_parameter_group_name = aws_neptune_cluster_parameter_group.neptune_cluster_parameter_group.name

  tags = {
    Name = "NeptuneCluster"
  }
}

# Create a Neptune instance in the cluster
resource "aws_neptune_cluster_instance" "neptune_cluster_instance" {
  count                = 1
  identifier           = "neptune-instance-${count.index}"
  cluster_identifier   = aws_neptune_cluster.neptune_cluster.id
  instance_class       = "db.r5.large"
  promotion_tier       = 1

  neptune_parameter_group_name = aws_neptune_parameter_group.neptune_instance_parameter_group.name

  tags = {
    Name = "NeptuneInstance"
  }
}

# Create a custom parameter group for the Neptune instance
resource "aws_neptune_parameter_group" "neptune_instance_parameter_group" {
  family = "neptune1"

  parameter {
    name         = "neptune_enable_audit_log"
    value        = "1"
    apply_method = "pending-reboot"
  }

  tags = {
    Name = "NeptuneInstanceParameterGroup"
  }
}

# Define a security group to control access to the Neptune instance
resource "aws_security_group" "neptune_security_group" {
  name        = "neptune-security-group"
  description = "Security group for Neptune instance"
  vpc_id      = var.vpc_id  # Provide the VPC ID

  tags = {
    Name = "NeptuneSecurityGroup"
  }
}

# Allow inbound traffic to the Neptune instance
resource "aws_security_group_rule" "neptune_ingress_rule" {
  type        = "ingress"
  from_port   = 8182
  to_port     = 8182
  protocol    = "tcp"
  cidr_blocks = ["0.0.0.0/0"]  # Customize this to restrict access

  security_group_id = aws_security_group.neptune_security_group.id

  tags = {
    Name = "NeptuneIngressRule"
  }
}

# Variables
variable "subnet_ids" {
  description = "List of subnet IDs for the Neptune subnet group"
  type        = list(string)
  default     = []  # Provide your subnet IDs here
}

variable "vpc_id" {
  description = "VPC ID for the Neptune security group"
  type        = string
  default     = ""  # Provide your VPC ID here
}
```

### Notes
- Ensure you provide the `subnet_ids` and `vpc_id` variables with appropriate values.
- Customize the security group rules to allow appropriate traffic based on your requirements.
- Adjust the parameter groups as needed to fit your specific use case.

