The Terraform program below defines an AWS RDS option group named "option-group-pike" with the specified engine version and options. The program includes a provider configuration for AWS and the necessary IAM role to manage the RDS option group.

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = var.region
}

variable "region" {
  description = "The AWS region to deploy the resources"
  default     = "us-west-2"
}

resource "aws_iam_role" "rds_option_group_role" {
  name = "rds-option-group-role"

  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Action = "sts:AssumeRole"
        Effect = "Allow"
        Principal = {
          Service = "rds.amazonaws.com"
        }
      }
    ]
  })
}

resource "aws_iam_role_policy_attachment" "rds_option_group_policy" {
  policy_arn = "arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/service-role/AmazonRDSFullAccess"
  role       = aws_iam_role.rds_option_group_role.name
}

resource "aws_db_option_group" "option_group_pike" {
  name         = "option-group-pike"
  engine_name  = "sqlserver-ee"
  major_engine_version = "11.00"

  option {
    option_name = "SQLSERVER_AUDIT"
  }

  option {
    option_name = "TDE"
  }

  depends_on = [aws_iam_role_policy_attachment.rds_option_group_policy]
}
```

This Terraform configuration does the following:
1. Configures the AWS provider with a default region.
2. Creates an IAM role named `rds-option-group-role` with a trust policy allowing RDS to assume the role.
3. Attaches the `AmazonRDSFullAccess` policy to the IAM role.
4. Defines an RDS option group named `option-group-pike` with the SQL Server Enterprise Edition engine and major version 11.00.
5. Adds the `SQLSERVER_AUDIT` and `TDE` options to the option group.
6. Ensures the option group depends on the IAM role policy attachment to ensure proper permissions are in place.

