### Description
The Terraform program below sets up an AWS Lightsail instance as an origin server and configures an AWS Lightsail distribution to route traffic to this instance. The distribution depends on the instance being available, ensuring that the origin server is ready before the distribution is set up.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-east-1"  # Specify your desired AWS region
}

variable "instance_name" {
  description = "The name of the Lightsail instance"
  type        = string
  default     = "my-lightsail-origin-instance"
}

variable "instance_blueprint_id" {
  description = "The blueprint ID for the Lightsail instance"
  type        = string
  default     = "ubuntu_22_04"
}

variable "instance_bundle_id" {
  description = "The bundle ID for the Lightsail instance"
  type        = string
  default     = "nano_1_0"
}

variable "distribution_name" {
  description = "The name of the Lightsail distribution"
  type        = string
  default     = "my-lightsail-distribution"
}

resource "aws_lightsail_instance" "lightsail_origin_instance" {
  name              = var.instance_name
  availability_zone = "us-east-1a"  # Specify your desired availability zone
  blueprint_id      = var.instance_blueprint_id
  bundle_id         = var.instance_bundle_id
}

resource "aws_lightsail_distribution" "lightsail_distribution" {
  name               = var.distribution_name
  origin             = aws_lightsail_instance.lightsail_origin_instance.public_ip
  default_cache_behavior {
    behavior = "cache"
  }
  cache_behavior {
    path               = "/*"
    behavior           = "cache"
    cached_http_methods = ["GET", "HEAD", "OPTIONS"]
    allowed_http_methods = ["GET", "HEAD", "OPTIONS", "PUT", "PATCH", "POST", "DELETE"]
    forwarded_cookies  = "whitelist"
    forwarded_headers  = "whitelist"
    forwarded_query_strings = true
  }
  depends_on = [aws_lightsail_instance.lightsail_origin_instance]
}
```

### Explanation
- **Provider Configuration**: The AWS provider is configured with a default region (`us-east-1`). You can change this to your preferred region.
- **Variables**: Several variables are defined to allow customization of the instance and distribution names, blueprint ID, and bundle ID.
- **Lightsail Instance**: An AWS Lightsail instance is created using the specified blueprint and bundle. The instance name is derived from the `instance_name` variable.
- **Lightsail Distribution**: An AWS Lightsail distribution is created, routing traffic to the public IP address of the Lightsail instance. The distribution includes default and custom cache behaviors.
- **Dependencies**: The distribution resource depends on the instance resource, ensuring that the instance is created before the distribution.

This configuration ensures that the Lightsail distribution is properly set up to route traffic to the specified origin instance.

