### Description
This Terraform program creates an S3 Glacier vault and sets up an SNS topic to receive notifications when archive retrievals are completed. The program includes an SNS topic subscription and an S3 bucket notification configuration to ensure that notifications are sent to the specified SNS topic.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"  # Specify your desired AWS region
}

resource "aws_s3_glacier_vault" "s3_glacier_vault" {
  name = "my_archive_vault"
}

resource "aws_sns_topic" "archive_retrieval_notification_topic" {
  name = "archive-retrieval-notification-topic"
}

resource "aws_sns_topic_subscription" "archive_retrieval_notification_subscription" {
  topic_arn = aws_sns_topic.archive_retrieval_notification_topic.arn
  protocol  = "email"  # Change to your preferred protocol (e.g., email, sms, http)
  endpoint  = "example@example.com"  # Replace with your actual endpoint
}

resource "aws_s3_bucket_notification" "s3_bucket_notification" {
  bucket = aws_s3_glacier_vault.s3_glacier_vault.name

  topic {
    topic_arn     = aws_sns_topic.archive_retrieval_notification_topic.arn
    events        = ["s3:GlacierRetrievalCompleted"]
    filter_suffix = ".txt"  # Optional: Filter by file suffix
  }
}
```

### Notes
- Ensure that the IAM role or user executing these Terraform configurations has the necessary permissions to create S3 Glacier vaults, SNS topics, and S3 bucket notifications.
- The SNS topic subscription can be configured to send notifications to various endpoints such as email, SMS, or HTTP(S).
- Adjust the `region`, `protocol`, `endpoint`, and `filter_suffix` as needed for your specific use case.

