### Description

This Terraform program creates an AWS Application Load Balancer (ALB) with a listener that handles incoming HTTP requests on port 80. It includes a listener rule with an Authenticate-OIDC action, which requires an OIDC provider to be configured and accessible. The program ensures that all resources are created in the correct order and that dependencies are properly managed.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

resource "aws_lb" "example_lb" {
  name               = "example-alb"
  internal           = false
  load_balancer_type = "application"

  subnets          = ["subnet-12345678", "subnet-87654321"]
  security_groups  = ["sg-12345678"]
  enable_deletion_protection = false
}

resource "aws_lb_listener" "example_listener" {
  load_balancer_arn = aws_lb.example_lb.arn
  protocol          = "HTTP"
  port              = "80"

  default_action {
    type             = "fixed-response"
    fixed_response {
      content_type = "text/plain"
      message_body = "Hello, World!"
      status_code  = "200"
    }
  }
}

resource "aws_lb_listener_rule" "example_listener_rule" {
  listener_arn = aws_lb_listener.example_listener.arn
  priority     = 1

  condition {
    field  = "host-header"
    values = ["example.com"]
  }

  action {
    type             = "authenticate-oidc"
    authenticate_oidc {
      authorization_endpoint = "https://example-idp.com/auth"
      client_id              = "client-id"
      client_secret          = "client-secret"
      issuer                 = "https://example-idp.com"
      token_endpoint         = "https://example-idp.com/token"
      user_info_endpoint     = "https://example-idp.com/userinfo"
    }
  }
}

resource "aws_lb_listener_rule_action" "example_authenticate_oidc_action" {
  # This resource is not necessary as the authenticate-oidc action is defined directly in the listener rule.
  # However, if you need to manage this separately, you can uncomment and configure it accordingly.
}
```

### Notes

1. **OIDC Provider Configuration**: Ensure that the OIDC provider (`authorization_endpoint`, `client_id`, `client_secret`, `issuer`, `token_endpoint`, `user_info_endpoint`) is properly configured and accessible.
2. **Subnets and Security Groups**: Replace the placeholder subnet and security group IDs with actual values from your AWS account.
3. **Region**: The provider is set to `us-west-2`. You can change this to any other region as needed.
4. **Deletion Protection**: The load balancer has deletion protection disabled by default. You can enable it if required.

This configuration ensures that the load balancer, listener, listener rule, and Authenticate-OIDC action are created in the correct order and with the necessary dependencies.

