### Description
This Terraform program sets up a VPC peering connection between two AWS Virtual Private Clouds (VPCs). The first VPC, named "peer," is configured with a CIDR block of `10.0.0.0/24`, and the second VPC, named "base," has a CIDR block of `10.1.0.0/24`. The peering connection, named "pike," allows these two VPCs to communicate with each other as if they were in the same network.

### Terraform HCL Program
```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"  # Ensure this is set to your desired AWS region
}

resource "aws_vpc" "peer" {
  cidr_block = "10.0.0.0/24"
  tags = {
    Name = "peer"
  }
}

resource "aws_vpc" "base" {
  cidr_block = "10.1.0.0/24"
  tags = {
    Name = "base"
  }
}

resource "aws_vpc_peering_connection" "pike" {
  vpc_id      = aws_vpc.peer.id
  peer_vpc_id = aws_vpc.base.id
  auto_accept = true  # Automatically accept the peering connection

  tags = {
    Name = "pike"
  }
}
```

